  /* ---------------------------------------------------- the title card ----
     r12 (21): large type over the planet for one stop, 400 ms in, 1.6 s held,
     500 ms out. Every word of it is also in the rail and in the status line,
     so the plate is aria-hidden and carries nothing of its own. The arrival
     (r12 (22)) is the same surface held for the length of the boot window. */
  /* r19g (11): the arrival line holds the same plate for the length of the
     boot window, and the first stop arrives inside it, so the one card that
     tells a visitor what they have just flown to was the one card no visitor
     ever saw. A title card that lands while the arrival line stands is not
     dropped and does not shove the arrival aside: it WAITS, with its own hold,
     and runs the moment the arrival line lets the plate go. One deep, because
     a second stop's card supersedes the first the same way it would on
     screen. */
  /* r19k (7): and it ANSWERS whether the plate is announcing this text, so
     the caller knows whether the rail's head has to wait for it. A queued card
     counts: it is announced late, but it is announced, and the head waits for
     the card that actually carries the name rather than for the arrival line
     standing in front of it. */
