  /* ---- r22 (P2): A LAYOUT PASS IS FOR A CHANGE OF SHAPE ------------------
     `layout` places every plate on the page against every other, which is
     about 150 layout reads. It was called at the end of every plate paint,
     which is every caption beat and every hop countdown: 141 of 2,056 frames
     in an 80 s hands-off watch took between 1 and 156 of them, for a plate
     whose boxes are constants and cannot have moved.

     So the paint asks only when the SHAPE has changed: a plate shown or
     hidden, a class that folds it, the key opened, a card up, the queue
     expanded, the panel's own state. Everything else is words inside boxes
     that were already placed. Every other caller of `layout` (a resize, a
     lens switch, a card, the tier note, the panel's reveal) is untouched. */
  /* only the classes that change a BOX belong in the signature. The plate
     also wears `--hop` and `--found`, which are a wrap rule and a tint, and
     both of them changed several times a minute: 18 layout passes in 45 s for
     a plate that had not moved a pixel. */
