  /* ---- r19p (10): A PHONE STOP IS SEEN ABOVE THE SHEET -------------------
     The renderer centres its look-at point at the viewport's own centre, and
     on a phone the rail sheet starts well above that, so a point subject at a
     stop landed UNDER the plate naming it and the only label on screen was
     another subject's (dark-J-P16). `ObsGlobe.setViewBias` moves the aim; the
     PAGE decides where, because the sheet is the page's. The aim goes to the
     middle of the band the sheet leaves, and the bias is cleared the moment
     the sheet is not covering anything (a desktop, a folded sheet, a card in
     its place), so every other camera state is exactly what it was. */
